\mt1 Jude
\c 1
\s1 A Greeting from Jude
\r (\ref James 1:1|JAS 1:1\ref*)
\p \v 1 Jude, a servant of Jesus Christ and a brother of James,
\p To those who \add are\add* called, loved by God \add the\add* Father, and kept in Jesus Christ:
\p \v 2 Mercy, peace, and love be multiplied to you.
\s1 God’s Judgment on the Ungodly
\r (\ref 2 Peter 3:1–7|2PE 3:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 3 Beloved, \add although\add* I made every effort to write to you about the salvation we share, I felt it necessary to write \add and\add* urge you to contend earnestly for the faith entrusted once for all to the saints. \v 4 For certain men have crept in \add among you\add* unnoticed — ungodly \add ones\add* who were designated long ago for condemnation. They turn the grace of our God into a license for immorality, and they deny our only Master and Lord, Jesus Christ.
\p \v 5 Although you are fully aware of this, I want to remind you that after Jesus\f + \fr 1:5 \ft NE, WH, BYZ, and TR \fqa the Lord\f* had delivered \add His\add* people out of \add the\add* land of Egypt, He destroyed those who did not believe. \v 6 And \add the\add* angels who did not stay within their \add own\add* domain but abandoned their \add proper\add* dwelling— \add these\add* He has kept in eternal chains under darkness, \add bound\add* for judgment on \add that\add* great day. \v 7 In like manner, Sodom and Gomorrah and the cities around them, who indulged in sexual immorality and pursued strange flesh, are on display as an example of those who sustain \add the\add* punishment of eternal fire.
\p \v 8 Yet in the same way these dreamers defile \add their\add* bodies, reject authority, and slander glorious \add beings\add*. \v 9 But \add even\add* the archangel Michael, when he disputed with the devil over the body of Moses, did not presume to bring a slanderous charge \add against him\add*, but said, “\add The\add* Lord rebuke you!”\f + \fr 1:9 \ft This account is attributed by Origen to the Testament of Moses, also called the Assumption of Moses.\f* \v 10 These \add men\add*, however, slander what they do not understand, and like irrational animals, they will be destroyed by the things they do instinctively. \v 11 Woe to them! They have traveled the path of Cain; they have rushed for profit into the error of Balaam; they have perished in Korah’s rebellion.
\p \v 12 These \add men\add* are hidden reefs\f + \fr 1:12 \ft Or \fqa are blemishes\f* in your love feasts, shamelessly feasting \add with you but\add* shepherding \add only\add* themselves. \add They are\add* clouds without water, carried along by \add the\add* wind; fruitless trees in autumn, twice dead after being uprooted. \v 13 \add They are\add* wild waves of \add the\add* sea, foaming up their \add own\add* shame; wandering stars, for whom blackest darkness has been reserved forever.
\p \v 14 Enoch, \add the\add* seventh from Adam, also prophesied about them:
\b 
\q1 “Behold, \add the\add* Lord is coming
\q2 with myriads of His holy \add ones\add*
\q2 \v 15 to execute judgment on everyone,
\q1 and to convict all the ungodly
\q2 of every ungodly act of wickedness
\q2 and every harsh \add word\add* spoken against Him by ungodly sinners.”\f + \fr 1:15 \ft See the First Book of Enoch (1 Enoch 1:9).\f*
\p \v 16 These \add men\add* are discontented grumblers, following after \add their\add* own lusts; their mouths spew arrogance; they flatter others for their own advantage.
\s1 A Call to Persevere
\r (\ref Hebrews 10:19–39|HEB 10:19-39\ref*; \ref 2 Peter 3:1–7|2PE 3:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 17 But you, beloved, remember what was foretold by the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ \v 18 when they said to you, “In \add the\add* last times there will be scoffers who will follow after their own ungodly desires.”\f + \fr 1:18 \ft See \ref 2 Peter 3:3|2PE 3:3\ref*.\f* \v 19 These are the \add ones who\add* cause divisions, \add who are\add* worldly \add and\add* devoid of \add the\add* Spirit.
\p \v 20 But you, beloved, by building yourselves \add up\add* in your most holy faith \add and\add* praying in \add the\add* Holy Spirit, \v 21 keep yourselves in \add the\add* love of God as you await the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ to bring \add you\add* eternal life.
\p \v 22 And indeed, have mercy on those who doubt; \v 23 save others by snatching \add them\add* from \add the\add* fire; and to still others show mercy \add tempered \add* with fear, hating even the clothing stained by the flesh.
\s1 Doxology
\r (\ref Romans 16:25–27|ROM 16:25-27\ref*)
\p \v 24 Now to Him who is able to keep you from stumbling and to present \add you\add* unblemished in His glorious presence, with great joy — \v 25 to \add the\add* only God our Savior \add be\add* glory, majesty, dominion, and authority through Jesus Christ our Lord before all time, and now, and for all eternity.
\p Amen.
